course: dictionary
lesson: 8894
title: Shrink: getting smaller
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Shrink means to get smaller, or to make something smaller. Read the words around it to check. «Clothes can shrink when they are washed in hot water» tells you a jumper can end up smaller after a hot wash.
explain: Shrink can also mean to move back because you are afraid. The clue is the fear. «Shrink away» from something means you pull back from it. In the cinema sentence, the pupil is the black dot in your eye, and it shrinks because the bright light makes your eye let in less light.
explain: Shrink can also be a noun, but it is informal. Here we will use it as a verb, a word for doing something. Its forms change with time: shrink now, shrinks for he or she, shrank in the past, and shrunk after have, as in «has shrunk».
explain: Maths and science use shrink too. «Arctic sea ice is shrinking because the world is getting warmer» means the ice is getting smaller as the weather warms. Check it in the sentence: if the ice got bigger, the sentence would not make sense.
fact: Shrink means to get smaller, or to make something smaller.
fact: The forms are shrink, shrinks, shrank (past), shrunk (after have), and shrinking.
fact: «Shrink» also means to move back because you are afraid, as in shrink away.
fact: In maths, the new size is the old size minus the change: «shrank to 25» gives the new size, and «shrank by 4» gives the change.
fact: Most things shrink when they get cold and grow when they get warm.
exercise: Clothes can shrink in a hot wash. What does shrink mean? | Move back in fear | Change colour | Get bigger, like rising dough | *Get smaller
exercise: «Walk out of a dark cinema into bright sunshine and you squint: the pupil shrinks fast.» What is the pupil doing? | *Getting smaller to let in less light | Closing its eyes | Getting bigger to see more | Glowing brightly
exercise: «The shape shrank to 25 cm, from 29 cm.» How much did the shape shrink by? | *4 cm | 54 cm | 29 cm | 25 cm
test: «Arctic sea ice is shrinking because the world is getting warmer.» What is happening to the sea ice? | Getting louder | *Getting smaller | Changing into sand | Getting taller
test: The kitten heard the dog bark and began to shrink away under the sofa. What does shrink away mean here? | Fall fast asleep | *Move back because it is scared | Move forward to say hello | Grow bigger and bigger
exam: «The bar shrank from 200 g to 180 g at the same price.» How much did the bar shrink by? | *20 g | 180 g | 200 g | 380 g
